# tools/r/region_stats_witness.rish -- a labeling's SIZE STRUCTURE, on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- image/regions.rye measures one Region per labeled component (its area and bounding box);
# this rung turns that measurement into a query: largest_region and smallest_region are the argmax/argmin picks (ties broken by
# the earliest label so the pick is deterministic), and size_histogram buckets every area into a size distribution whose last
# bucket absorbs the tail, so no big blob is ever dropped out of range.
#
# The crux this witness proves on metal: four components of areas 16, 9, 2, 1 give largest_region the 4x4 block (label one) and
# smallest_region the lone speck (label four); size_histogram over four buckets three wide reads 2, 0, 1, 1 (the last bucket
# absorbing area 16 past its edge), the counts summing to the region count; a one-bucket histogram absorbs every area; two
# equal-area specks make a tie both pickers break to the earliest label; refusals by name. No network, no key, no funds -- the
# size questions a surface names the day it sorts its blobs, on our own open geometry.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/r/region_stats_witness.rish

say "region_stats: Language EN -- Season G size-structure queries over a slice of measured regions; largest_region and smallest_region pick the extremes, size_histogram buckets the areas into a distribution the last bucket absorbs the tail of."
say "region_stats: Style Radiant -- compose not braid: this rung owns only the two reductions and the bucketing; regions owns the Region type and its area, the caller measures once and asks these questions over the slice it already holds. No gather, no blend, no codec, no color, not even a pixel loop."
say "region_stats: Lens TAME -- the bucket count is capped by region_stats_max_buckets so the counts slice can never grow past a named ceiling; an empty region slice refuses EmptyRegions and a zero bucket count or width refuses BadBucketing up front so a refusal allocates nothing; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/region_stats"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/region_stats.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "region_stats: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "region_stats: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "region_stats: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-region-stats" else "region_stats: selftest did not print the GREEN line"

say "region_stats: GREEN -- the largest pick takes the biggest blob and the smallest the lone speck, the histogram buckets the areas with the last bucket absorbing the tail, a tie breaks to the earliest label, the refusals fire by name, on metal."
